      "visualHeaderTooltip": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "text": {
              "expr": {
                "Literal": {
                  "Value": "'How to read. Zoom on March 2020: when volatility jumps, the Transformer stays below the other forecasts - accurate on average, too low when it matters. Bias: orange = forecasts too low on average (the dangerous side for risk), blue = too high; over long periods a small positive bias is normal. QLIKE punishes a forecast that is too low more than one that is too high. Cards and bars always compare all five forecasts, whatever models are selected.'"
                }
